by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-12T13:40:07Z

I reworked this and pushed on your branch, @SamuilovAD. Thanks for reporting the problem and for the patch, the diagnosis was right.

I took a different route: instead of a new `CAST_SCALAR_COLLECTIONS` option with its own casting rules, scalar collections now recurse into their elements the way object and union-typed collections already do. Each element goes through `validateAndDenormalize()`, so `ENABLE_TYPE_CONVERSION`, `FILTER_BOOL`, `DISABLE_TYPE_ENFORCEMENT`, nullability, the deserialization path in errors and `COLLECT_DENORMALIZATION_ERRORS` all apply with the single set of rules the rest of the component uses. Two options for the same conversion, with rules that differ in the details, would have been hard to keep in sync.

This also enforces the element type, which the previous behaviour did not: `int[]` receiving `'nope'` now throws, like the same value on a plain `int` property already did. That is why it targets 8.2 and not a patch branch.

Your commit is still in the branch history. Description and title updated.

